From 3ed76c0d2c1011926e89eed607dd51f84c5831d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: superc-agent <agent@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:52:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] superc extensions: defer, errdefer/err, test/-test,
 package/import, interface/impl, #macro with __local hygiene

All superc language extensions from docs/plan.md, gated behind TCC_EXT
(build with EXTRA-DEFS=-DTCC_EXT, enable per-TU with -std=tcc-ext, which
also defines __TCC_EXT__). Without the extension all new keywords are
un-interned again, so a plain build behaves exactly like upstream tcc.

- defer: runtime record stack plus a per-function dispatcher; scope,
  loop, break/continue/goto and return unwinding in LIFO order, the
  return value is spilled around the cleanups.
- errdefer/err: error slot, in-place cleanups and the -1 sentinel;
  'err();' re-raises an error handled one frame further down.
- test/-test/-test-filter: file-scope test blocks become static
  functions, the runner reports PASS/FAIL and the exit code.
- package/import: symbols are mangled as NAME__sym, imports resolve
  unqualified names, both single-TU and across translation units.
- interface/impl: fat pointer {void *self; const VT *vt;} plus a
  generated vtable object per impl; method calls are rewritten at the
  call site and struct values convert implicitly or with a cast.
- #macro/__local: hygienic macros; __local names are renamed with an
  expansion counter before arguments are substituted.

Tests: tests/tests2/156_superc_defer .. 161_superc_macro, enabled only
when the compiler was built with -DTCC_EXT. Full tests2 suite passes
with (140) and without (134) the extension.
